        RULES {
            #iQ7E0LHpZN78tvNOyPXuF2: ujik_nomad_tradition "Ujik Nomad Tradition: The Ujik of the Plains of Wind and Stone live as nomadic herders in social groups called ordu, traveling with their herds across a vast swath of the continent. Ujik riders are nearly unparalleled; indeed, the Unicorn Clan learned much about cavalry from the Ujik when the two groups first met centuries ago. As a result of the Ujik's influence, the Unicorn adopted technologies and tactics like stirrups and the feigned retreat that would make them the greatest riders in the Emerald Empire upon their return. However, a member of an Ujik ordu must be able to do much more than ride. Most Ujik have a wide array of skills needed for their way of living: martial skills to protect their animals from predators and raiders alike, interpersonal skills to navigate encounters with other groups upon the plains, knowledge of animal husbandry and weather patterns to know where to move their herds. Of course, traditions tend to vary by ordu—some of which are small family groups, others massive moving cities of interwoven alliances."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW ADVANTAGES (DISTINCTIONS)
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 93)
    #AGX4ZSa695HuAd5BMrm0Wj ^"Affinity with [Animal Type]" DEF {
        EXTENDS #L5R266oP8qR0sT2uV4wX6y ^"Distinction"

        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ring" STRING "Void"
            ^"Types" LIST ["Fame", "Interpersonal"]
        }

        EFFECT {
            "Sometime in the past, you assisted an animal in some way or saved its life. Now, any animal of that type you encounter gives you a little extra consideration, sparing you from its hunt or even helping you in return."
            "After performing a check when interacting with this specific type of animal (such as a Survival [Void] check to find food in wolf territory, if you have an affinity with wolves, or a Tactics [Void] check to cede territory to the enemy only to let the wolves overtake them), you may reroll up to two dice."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 93)
    #Yh2FO13lb5Hhsp27DHIPaf ^"Legal Scholarship" DEF {
        EXTENDS #L5R266oP8qR0sT2uV4wX6y ^"Distinction"

        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ring" STRING "Air"
            ^"Types" LIST ["Interpersonal", "Social"]
        }

        EFFECT {
            "Your family possesses old legal documents not only on Rokugani law but also from other cultures, such as Qamarist law, and perhaps even local, provincial laws, such as a village elder's edict not to use the well after midnight."
            "After performing a check when interacting with some legal body or using a legal code (such as a Government [Air] check to use an obscure Qamari law regarding land rights or a Commerce [Air] check to use an old Ujik agreement to renegotiate a trade), you may reroll up to two dice."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 93)
    #fqzCFgXawRTXuiEPo4sowU ^"Syncretic Philosophy" DEF {
        EXTENDS #L5R266oP8qR0sT2uV4wX6y ^"Distinction"

        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ring" STRING "Water"
            ^"Types" LIST ["Interpersonal", "Mental"]
        }

        EFFECT {
            "Having studied or been brought up exposed to many cultures, philosophies, and religious practices, you can understand the nuances of a person's (or your own) moral stance and ethical decisions when you speak with them."
            "After performing a check to appeal to someone's personal sense of ethics, morality, or philosophy (such as a Performance [Water] check to convince an angry group to spare someone's life or a Meditation [Water] check to reexamine your own frustrating situation), you may reroll up to two dice."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW ADVANTAGES (PASSIONS)
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 94)
    #o30KnaWjpTlZxkSIzCOOHI ^"Horse Racing" DEF {
        EXTENDS #L5R267zA9bC1dE3fG5hI7j ^"Passion"

        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ring" STRING "Air"
            ^"Types" LIST ["Physical"]
        }

        EFFECT {
            "You do not enjoy just the speed of racing but also the bond of horse and rider coming together in competition. You (and your horse) understand how racing requires skill, perception, and endurance."
            "After performing a check to push your horse or steed to its limits (such as a Fitness [Air] check to duck and weave on the polo field or a Survival [Air] check to get your horse to rush down a frightening or dangerous path), you remove 3 strife."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 94)
    #DFcGhskrhubdikFxEfJy4G ^"Hot Pot" DEF {
        EXTENDS #L5R267zA9bC1dE3fG5hI7j ^"Passion"

        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ring" STRING "Earth"
            ^"Types" LIST ["Interpersonal", "Physical"]
        }

        EFFECT {
            "You know how to prepare a good, hearty, flavorful meal in a communal environment. You can identify the meats, tubers, vegetables, and spices to make hot pot, as well as what might spoil or be poisonous to the meal. Because of the strong associations, you can also recall memories connected to sharing hot pot with friends and family."
            "After performing a check involving the preparation of a communal meal of hot pot (such as a Labor [Earth] check to stretch limited rations into a satisfying meal or a Courtesy [Earth] check to make a guest feel disarmed and at ease over dinner), you remove 3 strife."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 94)
    #GMRte1Waqs08wm7GBE1DGM ^"Stargazing" DEF {
        EXTENDS #L5R267zA9bC1dE3fG5hI7j ^"Passion"

        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ring" STRING "Void"
            ^"Types" LIST ["Mental", "Spiritual"]
        }

        EFFECT {
            "You can use the stars not only to navigate but also to tell the time, be it hour or season. You also know many astrological myths and stories related to heavenly phenomena such as meteor showers, supernovae, comets, and constellations."
            "After performing a check to recall an astronomical fact (such as a Theology [Void] check to interpret whether a specific comet means doom or blessing or a Composition [Void] check to layer double meaning into a poem using a reference to a constellation), you remove 3 strife."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW DISADVANTAGES (ADVERSITIES)
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 95)
    #vCWvYEgXrgamwexXh92Pb3 ^"Lost Family History" DEF {
        EXTENDS #L5R268kL0mN2oP4qR6sT8u ^"Adversity"

        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ring" STRING "Earth"
            ^"Types" LIST ["Interpersonal", "Material"]
        }

        EFFECT {
            "At some point, your family had an important historical record, whether scrolls and books, songs and poems, or a family genealogical chart or registry. Some event or catastrophe caused your family to lose these records. Your family may still have other records, so perhaps only a certain set has been lost."
            "When you make a check to recall or find something related to your lost history (such as a Culture [Earth] check to remember if your family ever dealt directly with a Hantei family member or a Skulduggery [Earth] check to remember if your family has ever dealt with a criminal organization), you must choose and reroll two dice containing (su) or (ex). After resolving the check, if you failed, you gain 1 Void point."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 95)
    #RbDh0TO6rg05DRO6FsXTFj ^"Penalty" DEF {
        EXTENDS #L5R268kL0mN2oP4qR6sT8u ^"Adversity"

        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ring" STRING "Fire"
            ^"Types" LIST ["Infamy", "Social"]
        }

        EFFECT {
            "You or your family have been charged with a minor offense, expressed as a fine or penalty you must pay to the aggrieved party over an extended period of time. The penalty is not necessarily the consequence of a crime; it could instead be part of an agreement for recompense to avoid further legal interference. The penalty most likely does not involve money and requires delivering material or symbolic goods, such as providing a magnificent horse or writing a set of humbling sutras."
            "When you make a check to avoid fulfilling the terms of the penalty (such as a Performance [Fire] check to publicly petition the aggrieved party to temporarily waive the penalty or a Theology [Fire] check to elicit a sign from the kami indicating how to absolve yourself of the penalty), you must choose and reroll two dice containing (su) or (ex). After resolving the check, if you failed, you gain 1 Void point."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 96)
    #wB4aW3rIzT9ZOs2lF3ZWgm ^"Schism in Status" DEF {
        EXTENDS #L5R268kL0mN2oP4qR6sT8u ^"Adversity"

        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ring" STRING "Water"
            ^"Types" LIST ["Infamy", "Interpersonal"]
        }

        EFFECT {
            "You have a vastly lower status with a specific social group, either imagined or actual. The members of this group treat you as if your status value were 20 points lower. While your feelings toward this group may be friendly, neutral, or antagonistic, it has no bearing on how they perceive you. You can try to improve the relationship by reducing the status gap, but it does not change your overall status value."
            "When you make a check to convince a member of this social group to listen to you (such as a Courtesy [Water] check to convince some artists to allow you to join their studio or a Commerce [Water] check to make a trade with a set of merchants), you must choose and reroll two dice containing (su) or (ex). After resolving the check, if you failed, you gain 1 Void point."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW DISADVANTAGES (ANXIETIES)
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 96)
    #IaeLyNJTmtwSL1JMLyz4tO ^"Animal Signs" DEF {
        EXTENDS #L5R269vW1xY3zA5bC7dE9f ^"Anxiety"

        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ring" STRING "Void"
            ^"Types" LIST ["Mental", "Spiritual"]
        }

        EFFECT {
            "You assign supernatural meaning to animal behavior."
            "After performing a check to interpret the actions of an animal (such as a Survival [Void] check to see if the caw of a crow portends good luck or bad, or a Medicine [Void] check to see if a rat's behavior signifies the presence of a plague), you receive 3 strife. If this is the first time this has occurred this scene, you gain 1 Void point."
        }
    }

    #N3VLk2Tx7sumN669NSOk5i ^"Disdain for Urban Sprawl" DEF {
        EXTENDS #L5R269vW1xY3zA5bC7dE9f ^"Anxiety"

        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ring" STRING "Earth"
            ^"Types" LIST ["Mental"]
        }

        EFFECT {
            "You dislike dense urban areas."
            "After performing a check to overcome some facet of city life (such as a Government [Earth] check to recall a burdensome or complicated local city law or a Tactics [Earth] check fighting in the tight, cluttered alleyways of a city), you receive 3 strife. If this is the first time this has occurred this scene, you gain 1 Void point."
        }
    }

    #ap1yY0Fuo1k4JYA1bEG1hA ^"Tip of the Tongue" DEF {
        EXTENDS #L5R269vW1xY3zA5bC7dE9f ^"Anxiety"

        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ring" STRING "Air"
            ^"Types" LIST ["Mental"]
        }

        EFFECT {
            "You know more than one language, perhaps several, and are fluent in all of them. So fluent that your mind mixes and matches words from all of them. While it does not hinder you socially, you find this frustrating when you cannot come up with that word you definitely know."
            "After performing a check to communicate that requires you to bridge cultural, religious, philosophical, or regional differences (such as a Courtesy [Air] check to use veiled wordplay or metaphors to smooth out a dispute between the samurai and bonge or a Theology [Air] check to explain an equivalent religious idea from another culture), you receive 3 strife. If this is the first time this has occurred this scene, you gain 1 Void point."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW SAMURAI HERITAGES
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 97)
    #NP4heHNcsR6nzDu4wiWVHa ^"New Samurai Heritages Table" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]

        HERITAGE_TABLE {

            1 #gCFkEdJN0NrsGSzFVhq6hD ^"Ancestral Horse Line" DEF {

                MODIFIERS {
                    ^"Glory" "+3"
                }

                EFFECT {
                    "You add an additional warhorse to your starting items. Roll a ten-sided die again to determine the horse's original family (1–2: Utaku horse, 3–4: Shinjo horse, 5–6: Iuchi horse, 7–8: Ide horse, 9–10: Moto horse). New horse options can be found beginning on page 141."
                }

                SUB_TABLE "1d10" {
                    "1-2" "Utaku"
                    "3-4" "Shinjo"
                    "5-6" "Iuchi"
                    "7-8" "Ide"
                    "9-10" "Moto"
                }
            }

            2 #L8URXctUSTs5q0RApULhPA ^"Heart of the Horse" DEF {

                MODIFIERS {
                    ^"Glory" "+3"
                    ^"Status" "-3"
                }

                EFFECT {
                    "You gain a horse (if you did not start with one), and you gain the Karmic Tie (Void) distinction (see page 108 of the core rulebook) with it."
                }
            }

            3-4 #KuGEkb3AAlrQ8DeDK8IIEU ^"Knowledge Exchange" DEF {

                MODIFIERS {
                    ^"Glory" "-5"
                }

                EFFECT {
                    "You know one additional technique. Roll a ten-sided die again to determine the category (1–3: kata, 4–6: shūji, 7: ritual, 8: invocation, 9: kihō, 10: mahō or ninjutsu), then select one technique with a prerequisite of school rank 1 and learn that technique. You can perform that technique even if it is not normally allowed by your school."
                }

                SUB_TABLE "1d10" {
                    "1-3" "kata"
                    "4-6" "shūji"
                    "7" "ritual"
                    "8" "invocation"
                    "9" "kihō"
                    "10" "mahō or ninjutsu"
                }
            }

            5 #LwBH4oJuiMiuHceoWTSEXh ^"Lost Banner" DEF {

                MODIFIERS {
                    ^"Glory" "-5"
                }

                EFFECT {
                    "You gain the Indomitable Will distinction (see page 106 of the core rulebook). This can be assigned in excess of the normal limitations on advantages at character creation."
                }
            }

            6-7 #OhRxrHSJXkLU2pLpLipNRQ ^"Splintered Loyalties" DEF {

                MODIFIERS {
                    ^"Status" "-5"
                }

                EFFECT {
                    "Roll a ten-sided die again to determine the skill you learned from your other culture (1–2: Aesthetics, 3–4 Courtesy, 5–6: Culture, 7–8: Meditation, 9–10: Commerce). You gain +1 rank in that skill."
                }

                SUB_TABLE "1d10" {
                    "1-2" "Aesthetics"
                    "3-4" "Courtesy"
                    "5-6" "Culture"
                    "7-8" "Meditation"
                    "9-10" "Commerce"
                }
            }

            8 #M6OlywRl97YLVScUZemIx6 ^"Sacred Wilderness" DEF {

                MODIFIERS {
                    ^"Status" "+5"
                }

                EFFECT {
                    "You add an estate to your starting items somewhere within your clan's territory. When at your estate, you and your allies receive food, shelter, and medical care for free."
                }
            }

            9 #1skeeUyizts1f1x9yfAlBH ^"Spirit Companion" DEF {

                MODIFIERS {
                    ^"Status" "+3"
                    ^"Glory" "-3"
                }

                EFFECT {
                    "You know one additional technique. Roll a ten-sided die again to determine the category (1–3: kata, 4–6: shūji, 7: ritual, 8: invocation, 9: kihō, 10: mahō or ninjutsu), then select one technique with a pr erequisite of school rank 1 and learn that technique. You can perform that technique even if it is not normally allowed by your school."
                }

                SUB_TABLE "1d10" {
                    "1-2" "Air"
                    "3-4" "Water"
                    "5-6" "Earth"
                    "7-8" "Fire"
                    "9-10" "Void"
                }
            }

            10 #Vb7AlY2oJr6tr0FG7FRC8m ^"Spiritual Debt" DEF {

                MODIFIERS {
                    ^"Honor" "+3"
                    ^"Glory" "-3"
                }

                EFFECT {
                    "Roll a ten-sided die again to determine the spirit's ring (1–2: Fire, 3–4: Earth, 5–6: Water, 7–8: Air, 9–10: Void). You may increase the value of your matching ring by 1 and reduce the value of a different ring by 1 (this still cannot raise a ring above 3)."
                }

                SUB_TABLE "1d10" {
                    "1-2" "Fire"
                    "3-4" "Earth"
                    "5-6" "Water"
                    "7-8" "Air"
                    "9-10" "Void"
                }
            }
        }

        RULES {
            #hdO3MyyooHHe540dsmHf76: new_samurai_heritages "New Samurai Heritages: A variety of unique heritages arise from having a family lineage derived in part from the Unicorn's history. Even non-Unicorn characters may take on one of these heritages because their family has a connection to a place outside Rokugan or to the wilderness. Because of the Unicorn's unique connection to lands outside Rokugan, they have access to more syncretic or diverse heritages, whether for good or for ill.\n\nTable 2-1: New Samurai Heritages presents backgrounds for characters connected to the Unicorn or to lands outside Rokugan. This table can be used instead of Table 2-1: Samurai Heritage on page 96 of the core rulebook and should be employed in the same manner."
            #ujKXvoxyYwABzkPS01mIM8: ancestral_horse_line "Ancestral Horse Line: One of your ancestors possessed a mighty Unicorn warhorse, and now your family's line and the horse's line parallel each other."
            #CU0fhc8rITHVMPEaZDIf6x: heart_of_the_horse "Heart of the Horse: You did not choose your horse: it chose you. Now you have a supernatural bond with it. It has a mind of its own, however, so your relationship with the horse is reciprocal. Treat it well, and it will treat you well."
            #Hx6ikhwWymQnvx6kUs0yfU: knowledge_exchange "Knowledge Exchange: One of your ancestors learned the techniques of another school and has passed that knowledge down the generations, finally to you."
            #yQnGFOFkJDwgvSsaavBFZD: lost_banner "Lost Banner: Your family once possessed a banner that symbolically carries your family's spirit, but an ancestor lost it due to war, betrayal, deceit, or incompetence. Everyone in your family has sworn to find it."
            #VwwMv7Yl2AYXEppmqUeZqg: splintered_loyalties "Splintered Loyalties: Either your family is directly related to a non-Rokugani people; or you grew up in Khanbulak, on the border of Rokugan; or you were raised on the Plains of Wind and Stone. Your feelings of loyalty lie equally with the Unicorn and the Empire, but you also have some loyalty to this non-Rokugani group."
            #eCZZS8XeFeATMNXBg4lfFD: sacred_wilderness "Sacred Wilderness: One of your ancestors established an area on your family's lands as a protected, sacred wilderness."
            #HJWlZccUHJ9l1bR1aq25pC: spirit_companion "Spirit Companion: One of your ancestors made an agreement with a spirit for service, and that spirit has served your family for generations."
            #t9k2l5Q7QgIFPGR1Ysmgrm: spiritual_debt "Spiritual Debt: Your family owes a long-standing debt to a spirit. The spirit occasionally asks your family to perform tasks that may seem incomprehensible or even contrary to what your family, your clan, or the Empire wishes."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW WEAPONS
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 99)
    #S6ve2I5cVLuoXyG2PNAiqh ^"New Weapons" DEF {
        ENTRIES {
            # Table 2-2: New Melee Weapons - Axes
            #iac6YFDGeepPExaHd2H6MA ^"Ganzu Ring Ax" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Melee (Ax)"
                ^"Skill" STRING "Martial Arts [Melee]"
                ^"Range" STRING "1-2"
                ^"Damage" INTEGER 4
                ^"Deadliness" INTEGER 7
                ^"Grip" STRING "2-hand"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Cumbersome", "Hewing", "Wargear"]
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 9
                ^"Price" STRING "35 koku"
                ^"Description" STRING "Among the most unusual battle-axes brandished by warriors of the Hidden Valley's Ganzu people, the ring ax is a large, bladed disk affixed to a two-handed shaft. Associated with guardians of the Sand Road, the ring ax has a disk-shaped blade. It is wielded in a martial style that utilizes the momentum of each strike so as to conserve energy. Unicorn Clan samurai sometimes call this weapon a coin ax due to the blade's resemblance to a Rokugani coin."
            }

            # Table 2-2: New Melee Weapons - Hand Weapons
            #54U34adoirzDFpaedl0Et2 ^"Katar (Punch Dagger)" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Melee (Hand Weapon)"
                ^"Skill" STRING "Martial Arts [Melee]"
                ^"Range" STRING "0-1"
                ^"Damage" INTEGER 3
                ^"Deadliness" INTEGER 5
                ^"Grip" STRING "1-hand"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Hewing", "Razor-Edged"]
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 8
                ^"Price" STRING "10 koku"
                ^"Description" STRING "Widely adopted throughout the nations surrounding the Sand Road and standard armament among the Ganzu people, the katar is a large, triangular dagger that is wielded in an H-shaped horizontal grip, with a guard protecting the knuckles. Often worn in pairs (khatari), this weapon has a wedge-shaped blade designed not only for slashing but also specifically for splitting and punching through shields and hardened armor."
            }

            # Table 2-2: New Melee Weapons - Polearms
            #GVjNbLjC4lRwKenJdIUhgt ^"Charging Lance" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Melee (Polearm)"
                ^"Skill" STRING "Martial Arts [Melee]"
                ^"Range" STRING "1-2"
                ^"Damage" INTEGER 4
                ^"Deadliness" INTEGER 3
                ^"Grip" STRING "2-hand"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Cumbersome", "Wargear"]
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 6
                ^"Price" STRING "7 koku"
                ^"Description" STRING "While relatively uncommon in Rokugan, lances are sometimes used where flat lands make unified cavalry charges a viable option for battle. The lance is a specialized spear designed exclusively for use on horseback, either to break the enemy in an initial charge or to hurl from horseback like a javelin.\n\nWhile most warriors favor the flexibility of the spear over the lance, Moto tactics make extensive use of cavalry lancers, usually to capitalize on openings created by archers. Enemies who break formation and spread to avoid arrows simply play into the Moto's hands, as they are now perfect fodder for the lancers' backbreaking charge."
                ^"Special" STRING "2-hand (after a Move action on horseback): Damage +3, Deadliness 7, gain the Hewing item quality (page 116)\n\n2-hand (thrown): Martial Arts [Ranged], Range 2–3"
            }
            #uOC2G3cRfiiE2gU3komYLS ^"Saddle Cutter" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Melee (Polearm)"
                ^"Skill" STRING "Martial Arts [Melee]"
                ^"Range" STRING "0-1"
                ^"Damage" INTEGER 4
                ^"Deadliness" INTEGER 6
                ^"Grip" STRING "1-hand"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Cumbersome", "Wargear"]
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 8
                ^"Price" STRING "15 koku"
                ^"Description" STRING "Among the many lessons the Ujik taught the Ki-Rin during their initial raids on Shinjo's clan was to remove any advantage the enemy believed they had. The Ujik saddle cutter is one such combat equalizer. This flexible, sharp, and serrated blade is designed to cut an opponent's stirrups while the wielder rides alongside them—or in skilled hands, to snip a saddle's straps, severing rider from steed. It is said that Utaku and Shinjo both hated this weapon and denounced it as underhanded and disrespectful, until Ide pointed out that when properly used, the weapon benevolently spares both horse and rider the bite of steel. Even so, few outside the Moto family or Ujik tribes practice its use today."
                ^"Special" STRING "When you make an attack with a saddle cutter, you may spend (op) as follows:\n\n(op)+: This attack deals no damage to the target; instead, it severs the target's stirrups, saddle, or other connection to their mount. The target must succeed on a TN 2 Fitness (Earth or Water) check to remain mounted. The TN of this check increases by a number equal to the number of (op) spent."
            }

            # Table 2-3: New Ranged Weapons - Crossbows
            #z32nOFuuCZV8TaiqR7tzei ^"Repeating Crossbow" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Ranged (Crossbow)"
                ^"Skill" STRING "Martial Arts [Ranged]"
                ^"Range" STRING "2-4"
                ^"Damage" INTEGER 5
                ^"Deadliness" INTEGER 3
                ^"Grip" STRING "2-hand"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Cumbersome"]
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 8
                ^"Price" STRING "50 koku"
                ^"Description" STRING "While the repeating crossbow is utilized along the length of the Sand Road, it is rarely seriously considered for battlefield deployment. Instead, it is typically used for home defense, at sea, and by the guards of al-Zawira. It has weaker projectiles and a shorter range than the standard crossbow, but it makes up for this with a wooden quarrel stock that reloads the crossbow after every draw, provided there is ammunition available (maximum 4 bolts). It is also small enough to be spanned by hand instead of by foot or special mechanism. It is said that this device inspired the invention of the Kaiu no oyumi (rapid-fire crossbow) in the last century."
            }

            # Table 2-3: New Ranged Weapons - Bows
            #GNQ51UnKfdHdMc4epJf7FB ^"Catalpa Bow" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Ranged (Bow)"
                ^"Skill" STRING "Martial Arts [Ranged]"
                ^"Range" STRING "2-5"
                ^"Damage" INTEGER 5
                ^"Deadliness" INTEGER 3
                ^"Grip" STRING "2-hand"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Ceremonial", "Sacred"]
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 7
                ^"Price" STRING "25 koku"
                ^"Description" STRING "Shrine folklore holds that the mere pluck of a bowstring can banish ghosts, and that yumi made from the tonewood of the catalpa tree are especially attractive to elemental spirits and repellent to malicious ones. The Kitsune Forest is rich with soft catalpa wood, which the Fox Clan uses for bow making (among other things). The Fox regularly trade catalpa yumi to the Phoenix Clan's Kaito family, for whom the wood is relatively rare. However, the Fox are careful to utilize catalpa only from trees that have fallen naturally; they believe that hewing catalpa will \"frighten\" the wood, reversing the effect of the sacred tone."
            }

            # Table 2-4: New Specialist Weapons
            #09jstHuw8IErYtqOevfmOH ^"Fire Lance (Polearm)" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Specialist (Polearm)"
                ^"Skill" STRING "Martial Arts [Melee]"
                ^"Range" STRING "2"
                ^"Damage" INTEGER 4
                ^"Deadliness" INTEGER 3
                ^"Grip" STRING "2-hand"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Cumbersome", "Prepare (firework only)", "Wargear"]
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 9
                ^"Price" STRING "40 koku"
                ^"Description" STRING "The use of black powder is strictly regulated in the Empire of Rokugan. While fireworks and certain demolitions are permitted, Imperial decree forbids this powder's use in weaponry or sieges. The Ganzu people are not bound by such decrees, deploying the fire lance as a means to defend the Sand Road from afar and as a cavalry countermeasure. In its most rudimentary form, the fire lance is a straight-flying firework attached to a polearm, but more advanced versions—like those with metal barrels or that fire pellets—are becoming more common.\n\nThe fire lance is a polearm when used as such. While its wielder is aiming the rocket, it counts as a ranged weapon."
                ^"Special" STRING "2-hand (firework launch): Martial Arts [Ranged], Range 3–5, Damage +3, Deadliness 9"
            }
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW SHIELDS
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 101)
    #m5fvvJVKSSHAU65XXDa7Pd ^"New Shields" DEF {
        # Shields are listed in Table 2-2 under the Shields category
        ENTRIES {
            #DkHpwKxwpdFllTnkPV9N4S ^"Ide Parasol Shield" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Shield"
                ^"Skill" STRING "Martial Arts [Melee]"
                ^"Range" STRING "0"
                ^"Damage" INTEGER 2
                ^"Deadliness" INTEGER 3
                ^"Grip" STRING "2-hand"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Concealed", "Cumbersome"]
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 9
                ^"Price" STRING "8 koku"
                ^"Description" STRING "An innovation of Ide family Imperial peacekeepers (and serving as their informal badge of office), the parasol shield is a folding rattan-cloth parasol with thin tin or brass plates hidden in the canopy, which is disguised beneath a layer of patterned silk. Considerably heavier than a typical parasol, a parasol shield is usually opened and stuck into the ground at an angle to provide cover, but it can also be used to protect against arrows. This parasol was invented to protect against bandit ambushes targeting diplomatic caravans."
                ^"Special" STRING "While this parasol shield's canopy is fully extended and readied, you treat your physical resistance as 3.\n\nAs a Movement and Support action, while the canopy is readied, you may increase the TN of the next Attack check targeting you by 1. This effect persists until the end of your next turn."
            }
            #aAZrjZOgZWW7rpJOskygOB ^"Standing Shield" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Shield"
                ^"Skill" STRING "Martial Arts [Melee]"
                ^"Range" STRING "0"
                ^"Damage" INTEGER 2
                ^"Deadliness" INTEGER 2
                ^"Grip" STRING "2-hand"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Cumbersome", "Durable"]
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 8
                ^"Price" STRING "12 koku"
                ^"Description" STRING "The standing shield is a heavy rectangular braced shield that is typically carried by a designated shield bearer, providing near-complete protection for both the bearer and the warrior behind them. Ashigaru bearing a standing shield are not permitted to retreat, as this would create gaps in the defense and expose their allies. These shields can also be propped to stand on their own, providing temporary cover on the battlefield."
                ^"Special" STRING "While you have a readied standing shield, or while it is deployed standing on its own in front of you, you treat your physical resistance as 6.\n\nAs a Movement and Support action, while you or a nearby bearer have the standing shield readied or deployed, you may increase the TN of Attack action checks made targeting you by 2. This effect persists until the start of your next turn, as long as you are behind the standing shield."
            }
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW ARMOR
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 103)
    #StzlLRBlzIz64w7L3We2WK ^"New Armor" DEF {
        # Table 2-5: New Armor
        ENTRIES {
            #whoR7B5vxmbWhxCdZvrd77 ^"Mirror Armor" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Armor"
                ^"Physical Resistance" INTEGER 3
                ^"Supernatural Resistance" INTEGER 1
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Wargear"]
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 8
                ^"Price" STRING "40 koku"
                ^"Description" STRING "A specialized type of riding armor, mirror armor consists of four rounded metal discs that are buffed and polished to a mirror shine, then integrated into a tunic made of overlapping metal and leather scales. They are accompanied by a rounded helm. The mirror plates are believed to not only protect the wearer from arrows but also to blind malicious spirits, deflecting their attention."
            }
            #xvBkoFKaDGaPHBVaiQk7Bi ^"Unicorn Barding" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Armor (Horse)"
                ^"Physical Resistance" INTEGER 2
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Ceremonial", "Resplendent", "Wargear"]
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 8
                ^"Price" STRING "65 koku"
                ^"Description" STRING "While most Rokugani war ponies are hindered in full barding, Unicorn barding utilizes several innovations to make armor lighter and more comfortable for the horse wearing it. Most barding is made from laminated plates set over a tent of padded cloth and includes a unique face covering similar to the war masks of samurai armor. Unicorn barding is generally considered superior, owing to better coverage, elaborate designs, and the care taken to ensure each piece of custom-made armor is comfortably fitted to the horse. Expensive and time-intensive to don, a suit of full Unicorn barding has become a status symbol for wealthy lords, worn more frequently in festivals and parades than for warfare.\n\nUnicorn barding can be worn only by horses, ponies, and other equine mounts."
            }
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW PERSONAL EFFECTS
    # ===========================

    #7XZGKSrwnxYpuYT03AutmY ^"New Personal Effects" DEF {
        ENTRIES {
            #5x2mlO4bElRYkIwPM7QxyM ^"Astrolabe" DEF {
                ^"Price" STRING "1 koku"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 8
                ^"Description" STRING "Among the most useful of pocket mathematical tools, astrolabes come in many forms, from a metal disk with shapes carved into its face; to a fist-sized globe with rotating rings interlocked along its body; and even to the mariner's astrolabe, which is held in both hands. The many functions of this tool include timekeeping, distance triangulation and estimation, mathematical calculation, and tracking the celestial bodies of the night sky."
            }
            #bxwzG4nAYorUoWsQ1GuRF9 ^"Horo (Arrow Cloak)" DEF {
                ^"Price" STRING "5 koku"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 6
                ^"Description" STRING "One of the oldest antiarrow innovations in Rokugan is the inflating arrow cloak, which is essentially a flexible, wicker-framed sail made of high-thread-count silk. Attached to a horseback rider at the waist and shoulders, the arrow cloak fills with air as the horse gallops, puffing out into a balloon shape. Arrows either bounce off the billowing cloak or are caught by the cloth before they can reach the rider. The arrow cloak has become a symbol of battlefield messengers and Imperial Heralds alike, but while it grants the rider significant protection from ranged attacks, it also makes them a target, as there is significant prestige in being the archer who killed an arrow cloak wearer."
                ^"Special" STRING "While wearing a deployed horo, treat your physical resistance against arrows and similar missiles as 5. While riding on horseback or otherwise mounted, increase this resistance to 6."
            }
            #rr6nqHvk4JKurWUu2KrKPU ^"Lantern (Personal)" DEF {
                ^"Price" STRING "1 bu"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 2
                ^"Description" STRING "Lanterns of all shapes and sorts are common throughout the Empire, and the craft of lantern making is considered one of Rokugan's greatest arts. The most typical personal lantern consists of a bamboo frame with paper stretched over the ribs to protect the candle within from the wind. Lanterns can be mounted on staves, carried by handles, hung from hooks, set to rest on stilts, or even designed to float on water. They can also be shaped like fantastic animals, painted, or formed from patterned paper. Metal or wooden lanterns are common as well, if a bit pricier."
            }
            #VxGHVrQENaEvysVeYtMyWY ^"Mineral-Oil Lamp" DEF {
                ^"Price" STRING "6 koku"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 8
                ^"Description" STRING "Most Rokugani personal lanterns use a candle as their light source, while standing and stone lanterns use rapeseed or sardine oil with a pith wick. Alchemists of the Qamarist Caliphate have used a refined oil made from coal and certain clays since long ago, and while only the purest of such oil burns clean enough to be used indoors, the resulting mineral-oil lamps burn brighter and longer than those that use whale or rapeseed oil. A mere vial of the \"glass naphtha\" can cost a farmer's yearly wage in Rokugan, and alchemists of several clans are secretly trying to reproduce it."
            }
            #IXbajLavVLkQgnbEkujNjz ^"Prayer Rug" DEF {
                ^"Price" STRING "2 koku"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 9
                ^"Description" STRING "One of the most important personal effects for those who worship the Nameless Prophet, the prayer rug is a thick carpet that is used for kneeling upon during daily prayers. Such rugs come in a wide variety of patterns, but all incorporate religious symbology of the Qamarist faith, aiding the user in their prayers."
            }
            #2W5yESVMQX9w39ni5tIwr2 ^"Sand Clock" DEF {
                ^"Price" STRING "2 koku"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 6
                ^"Description" STRING "Personal timepieces have become status symbols among the Rokugani elite, as traditional water clocks are larger, more common, and less expensive. The most prized timepieces are sand clocks, the best examples of which come from al-Zawira. They consist of two glass-bulb ampoules partially filled with powdered marble or ash, expertly measured so that it takes a certain amount of time for sand to pass from one bulb to the other. The glassblowing techniques required to make the sand clock are not exclusive to the artisans of the Caliphate, but access to better materials, the skill required to make smaller examples, and the artistic elegance typical of the devices have created a cottage industry in al-Zawira for sand clocks calibrated for the Rokugani hour."
            }
            #XiqsdS3TzVHutDp9ERqfD9 ^"Traveling Board Games" DEF {
                ^"Price" STRING "1 bu"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 4
                ^"Description" STRING "Games of luck and skill are popular throughout the world, and traveling versions are often carried on long trips. The most common are contained within hinged boxes, many of which fold out into a game board and contain the pieces required by the game. The most sophisticated may even use magnets to keep pieces from falling off the board, although these are exceptional examples. Most are simple games like Go; shōgi; sugoroku; or ones from distant lands, like hounds and jackals or senet. For some, playing a game can be a means to relax on a stressful trip, or even akin to personal meditation."
            }
            #NaWaRXK8YpytuQnOg85cjN ^"Word of the Prophet" DEF {
                ^"Price" STRING "15 koku"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 9
                ^"Description" STRING "While the Word of the Prophet is an illuminated tome that is banned within Rokugani borders, countless copies of it circulate along the Sand Road, and some have even made their way within the Emerald Empire's borders. The book, a collection of Qamarist stories, is the basis of worship for the Qamarist faith. It contains not only the story of the Nameless Prophet but also an extensive appendix of notes, discussions, and arguments by noted scholars. Although the contents are usually the same in each book, no two copies are identical, varying in their elaborate decorations, notes, and inscribed interpretations. When passed down as family heirlooms, they often contain family trees and mementos of family ancestors from long past."
            }
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # BLESSED TREASURES
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 104)
    #562ZiWkcgtrHe7XbyUPBLq ^"Talisman of the Sun" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Blessed Treasure (Unicorn)"
            ^"Description" STRING "During the Ki-Rin Clan's overthrow of the undead Sun Kings in Rempet alongside al-Qamari, a brave samurai heard a voice crying out to be freed from its prison. The source of these cries was a talisman of braided metal, bearing a jewel that shone like fire. The voice promised to aid its rescuers if only it could feel the sun again. It is said that after the Sun Kings' defeat, Iuchi made many attempts to free the imprisoned spirit from the talisman, as did his daughter and grandson after him, but to no avail. The Talisman of the Sun is now a treasure resting in Gatherer of Winds Castle, one of its many mysteries, brought out from its ornate container each morning by the seneschals to bask in the light of the sunrise."
            ^"Sealed Invocations" LIST OF STRING ["By the Light of the Lord Moon (core p192)", "Hands of the Tides (core p208)", "Wings of the Phoenix (core p206)"]
            ^"Special" STRING "After the talisman is used to cast an invocation, it cannot cast another until it has basked in sunlight for at least one minute. It does not have a stability value (see Stability, page 106)—for now, the spirit is trapped indefinitely."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 104)
    #uXjYpQa2tTLrN8KAHbzdu4 ^"Yuki: Ancestral Armor" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Blessed Treasure (Unicorn)"
            ^"Description" STRING "As the very armor that Shinjo wore when she left the Empire, Yuki would normally be considered one of the oldest examples of Rokugani armor. Yet over the centuries, the ancestral armor of the Unicorn Clan has seen many revisions and upgrades, even before it was finally gifted to Shinjo's son, Nishijin, before her confrontation with Orochi, the Great Serpent. On that day, Yuki's cream-white plates were painted midnight purple, a new regal color for a reborn clan. When the Unicorn returned, Yuki was unrecognizable with its white fur cloak, golden helmet-horns, and Qamari upgrades. But Shinjo's presence still lingers within, reminding the wearer of her promise to always return.\n\nWhile Yuki's base components are old-fashioned, many parts have been replaced over the years. The armor must be adjusted for each new champion, and each generation adds new improvements and embellishments. Thus, it has become a living embodiment of the Unicorn Clan's entire history, not merely its glorious past. It currently rests on display at Far Traveler Castle.\n\nYuki is an awakened suit of midnight-purple lacquered riding armor, adorned in white fur and gilded, modified to fit the current Unicorn Clan Champion."
            ^"Quirk" STRING "Yuki becomes impossible to remove while the armor senses danger is near."
            ^"Profile" STRING "Physical 6, Supernatural 2, Ceremonial, Cumbersome, Durable, Sacred, Wargear"
            ^"Sealed Invocation" STRING "Yuki has Nature's Touch (core rulebook, page 194) sealed within it, which the wearer may activate once per game session as an action, using Fitness (Air) instead of Theology (Air)."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 104)
    #samV1iksiXm5E2ITa8Msbc ^"Ancestral Sword of the Fox Clan" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Blessed Treasure (Fox)"
            ^"Description" STRING "As a part of the treaty that ended the Lion-Phoenix War and created the Fox Clan, the Emperor commissioned the forging of a grand sword to be presented to the Fox Clan Champion. Agasha family blacksmiths forged a splendid blade, and after consultations with the daimyō of the Yogo family, the sword was inscribed with spiritual wards. Shortly after accepting the gift, the Fox Clan Champion disregarded it, setting it aside to languish—to him, the sword was simply a reminder of all the Fox had lost at the hands of the Great Clans, an attempt to placate the guilty consciences of those who had failed his people. Nearly three centuries later, a Fox samurai accidentally discovered that the blade had been replaced with a forgery. Yet few seemed to care; many assumed the forest denizens had taken it, and no one could even recall the sword's name. The ancestral sword of the Fox Clan has remained lost ever since—or at least, no one has yet admitted to finding it.\n\nThe name of the ancestral sword of the Fox Clan is long forgotten. It is a tachi (see Celestial Realms, page 98) of exquisite quality."
            ^"Quirk" STRING "When a person holding the ancestral sword of the Fox says something they know to be false, they suffer a tremendous flash of pain. This also happens if the wielder knowingly hears a falsehood and does not correct it."
            ^"Profile" STRING "Range 1, Damage 5, Deadliness 7 (8 if wielded two-handed), Ceremonial, Cumbersome, Durable, Razor-Edged, Sacred"
            ^"Sealed Invocation" STRING "This sword has Vapor of Nightmares (core rulebook, page 195) sealed within it, which the wielder may activate once per game session as an action, using Martial Arts [Melee] (Air) instead of Theology (Air)."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 105)
    #b7VapMonpAwgTiFBNa0aV4 ^"Fox Pipe" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Blessed Treasure (Fox)"
            ^"Description" STRING "The common superstition among Fox Clan samurai that one must never discuss secrets when one can smell smoke might be owed to the belief in \"pipe foxes,\" ethereal spirits said to live within smoking pipes enchanted for this purpose. Such smoking pipes, which appear as ordinary kiseru that incorporate fox carvings on the bowl, are created as the result of a pact between a trickster spirit and a shugenja. Smoking the pipe causes an ethereal fox to rise from the bowl, ready to do the bidding of the smoker. This spirit is sent to spy on others unnoticed, reporting back to the smoker whatever it has heard. Folktales abound of lost fox pipes eventually making their way to market shops, where they are unknowingly purchased and the foxes within accidentally discovered. This is the origin of the Fox Clan colloquialism \"To smoke up a fox,\" meaning to discover something useful in something believed to be useless."
            ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Durable", "Sacred"]
            ^"Quirk" STRING "Smoking from this pipe causes a fox made of smoke to rise from the pipe, ready to spy for the smoker."
            ^"Sealed Invocation" STRING "This pipe has Secrets on the Wind (core rulebook, page 194) sealed within it. The invocation may be activated once per game session as an action by smoking the pipe and using Courtesy (Air) instead of Theology (Air) on the check made to activate it.\n\nWhen a Fox Pipe casts its sealed invocation, the TN is decreased by 1, you may target a position at Range 0–4, and it lasts until you have finished smoking the pipe."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # MEISHODO TALISMANS
    # ===========================

    #DLOXKQoyDWY0ZXH3FueINC ^"Meishōdō Talisman System" DEF {

        RULES {
            #qfsKZWYFMlZmEv1jcQ7Hs0: meishodo_talismans "Meishōdō Talismans: The core rulebook contains a simplified version of rules for meishōdō talismans in the Iuchi Meishōdō Master school ability, The Way of Names, on page 83. If a GM wishes to use more detailed rules for meishōdō talismans, they may use the following rules instead. If they do, the second paragraph of the Iuchi Meishōdō Master's school ability should be treated as reading: \"You can sustain a number of meishōdō talismans up to your school rank. If you create one or more meishōdō talismans in excess of this limit, you must choose a number up to your school rank and then release the spirits contained within the rest.\" All other parts of the ability are replaced by the rules here."
            #JOLH6lJcnIBMHhLBaehOHD: using_meishodo_talismans "Using Meishōdō Talismans: A character carrying a meishōdō talisman can perform any invocations sealed within it. To do so, they make a check to activate the invocation using their skill ranks and the sealed spirit's ring value in place of their own. They still keep a total number of dice equal to their own ring, however."
            #V95ekphaJxDwU6CRFoTTDT: creating_meishodo_talismans "Creating Meishōdō Talismans: A character who is a member of the Iuchi Meishōdō Master School or who has completed the Student of Names title (page 135) can create a meishōdō talisman by completing the Seal in an Object social objective (see page 128) during an otherworldly encounter (see page 125). This seals a spirit within the object. Once the talisman is made, the character determines the techniques it contains and its stability value."
            #fSokZQQBsNiIf6qoeR9VG0: techniques_contained "Techniques Contained: Meishōdō talismans are valuable because they contain techniques that can be accessed by any user, even one untrained in the Way of Names. To determine what technique is contained in a talisman, the creator of the talisman chooses one invocation matching the element of the highest ring of the sealed-in spirit. The rank of the invocation cannot exceed the value of the spirit's highest ring. If two or more rings are tied, the creator chooses one.\n\nIf the spirit is Tainted, the creator has the option of instead choosing one mahō technique in the same manner, with the same requirements.\n\nAny techniques chosen this way are the techniques contained in the talisman."
            #T9c3jxYocBM09u4rblm91g: stability "Stability: A meishōdō talisman also has a stability value. This value represents the likelihood that the spirit within will break free when the talisman is used. The stability value is determined at the time the talisman is created."
            #I9DbJfiRv4ukM7SBkNKMeT: determine_stability "Determine Stability: To determine a talisman's stability value, add the creator's excess momentum points from the Seal in an Object social objective (see page 128) to their ranks in Design. Then, subtract the spirit's ranks in the Scholar skill group (or Theology, if it has individual skills). This value, to a minimum of 1, is the starting stability value. The higher the stability value, the harder it is for the spirit to break free.\n\nIf the stability of a talisman ever reaches 0, the spirit within shatters the talisman and is unleased on the world."
            #o4rVMp4QOQ0bNwiCYdOxzD: losing_stability "Losing Stability: Stability can be lowered in several ways:\n\nIf the physical object that is the talisman ever gains the Damaged item quality, the stability value is reduced by 1. If it gains the Destroyed item quality, the stability value is reduced to 0.\n\nIf a technique from the talisman would otherwise cause the wielder to suffer the Afflicted condition, they do not suffer that condition, but the stability of the talisman is reduced by 1.\n\nWhen activating a technique from the talisman, if the wielder drops one or more (ring) containing (st) (op), the stability value is reduced by 1."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # ITEM PATTERNS
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 107)
    #Ivhn0HxMM1ze2hwuulqoJw ^"Item Patterns" DEF {
        ENTRIES {
            #970oSiGdYA3Igx5DUoraaL ^"Ujik Horsebow Pattern" DEF {
                ^"Effect" STRING "A bow made with the Ujik horsebow pattern gains +1 damage and the Snaring item quality due to its additional punching force. It loses the Durable item quality (and can never gain it), and if it is exposed to significant moisture, it gains the Damaged item quality."
                ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 4
                ^"Rarity Modifier" STRING "+3"
            }
            #7KfbGurtLXblPtL1OzulvV ^"Utsuko Pattern" DEF {
                ^"Effect" STRING "After it is used to capture a spirit, a meishōdō talisman with the Utsuko pattern increases its stability by its creator's Void ring."
                ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 3
                ^"Rarity Modifier" STRING "+4"
            }
            #qfEzdVuhHLyEkJPEg0oG5d ^"Watered Steel Pattern" DEF {
                ^"Effect" STRING "An item made primarily of watered steel gains the Durable and Resplendent item qualities; if it is a weapon that already has the Durable item quality, it instead gains +1 deadliness. Additionally, Razor-Edged weapons made of watered steel gain the Hewing item quality (see page 116).\n\nArmor cannot be made from watered steel."
                ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 8
                ^"Rarity Modifier" STRING "+6"
            }
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW ITEM QUALITY
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 116)
    #WkPB9Llu9RSfylXnGqc6yb ^"Hewing" DEF {

        RULES {
            #BjFyrXZAtTZJex0KKPmBnB: hewing "Hewing: This weapon is specifically designed to bypass or break through shields and armor.\n\nWhen you make an Attack action check with a Hewing weapon, you may spend (op) as follows:\n\n(op): This attack ignores any TN bonuses from an opponent's shield.\n\n(op)+: Decrease the target's physical resistance by 1 for each (op) spent this way."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW TECHNIQUES - KATA
    # ===========================

    # -- General Kata --

    # source stat block (page 108)
    #RDZZV3xdM4zfsyzuH0IQlj ^"Cautious Tread" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Kata"
            ^"Subtype" STRING "General"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 1
            ^"Activation" STRING "When you make a Movement action check while riding a mount, you may spend (op) as follows:"
            ^"Effects" STRING "(op)(op): Choose one of the following terrain qualities: Dangerous, Entangling, or Obscuring. You and your mount ignore its effects. This effect persists until the end of your next turn."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 108)
    #P15e2pQKH2HRNF35ToPRjd ^"Stalking Leopard Style" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Kata"
            ^"Subtype" STRING "General"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "When you make an Attack action check, you may spend (op) as follows:"
            ^"Effects" STRING "(op)(op): If you succeed and your target is Disoriented or Prone, treat the damage and deadliness of your weapon as increased by your ranks in Survival."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 108)
    #hQmJwXOpbHE6x5G3iVzBHW ^"Sudden Downpour Style" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Kata"
            ^"Subtype" STRING "General"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "When you make an Attack action check using a bow or polearm, if you are mounted, you may spend (op) as follows:"
            ^"Effects" STRING "(op)(op): If your target makes a check to resist an effect of this Attack action (including a check to resist a critical strike you inflict as part of the attack), increase the TN of that check by your mount's Water ring."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 108)
    #OnIk5kQH4WLN5QibiTeri2 ^"Swaying Grass Evasion" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Kata"
            ^"Subtype" STRING "General"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Movement and Support action, if you are in Dangerous, Entangling, or Obscuring terrain, you may receive a number of fatigue up to your ranks in Survival to duck into cover to avoid oncoming threats."
            ^"Effects" STRING "Increase the TN of Martial Arts [Ranged] checks targeting you by half the amount of fatigue you received this way (rounded up). This effect persists until the end of your next turn."
        }
    }

    # -- Close-Combat Kata --

    # source stat block (page 108)
    #WQZ0mllFAsJ3S0PskmmIXV ^"Distracting Flurry Style" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Kata"
            ^"Subtype" STRING "Close-Combat"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "When you make an Attack action check using Martial Arts [Melee] or Martial Arts [Unarmed], if you are in Dangerous, Entangling, or Obscuring terrain, you may spend (op) as follows:"
            ^"Effects" STRING "(op): If you fail, your target suffers the Disoriented condition."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 109)
    #0rlsYqqzYRaFjQFPLbnasp ^"Slashing Sandstorm Style" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Kata"
            ^"Subtype" STRING "Close-Combat"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "When you make an Attack action check using Martial Arts [Melee] while wielding an ax, you may spend (op) as follows:"
            ^"Effects" STRING "(op): If you succeed and your target is a minion, your target suffers additional damage equal to the deadliness of your weapon."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)+: If you fail and your target's ranks in Meditation are less than or equal to (op) spent this way, your target receives strife equal to the deadliness of your weapon."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 109)
    #ifPgIEejNoYh9GGArpjPXD ^"Scouring Wind Style" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Kata"
            ^"Subtype" STRING "Close-Combat"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "When you make an Attack action check using Martial Arts [Melee] or Martial Arts [Unarmed] while wielding a non-Razor-Edged weapon in two hands, you may spend (op) as follows:"
            ^"Effects" STRING "(op)(op): If you succeed, instead of dealing damage, choose one defensive item your target is using (such as armor they are wearing or a readied shield they are wielding). The item receives the Damaged item quality; if it is already Damaged, it becomes Destroyed instead."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op): If you succeed and you are wielding an ax, in addition to dealing damage, choose one defensive item your target is using (such as armor they are wearing or a readied shield they are wielding). It receives the Damaged item quality; if it is already Damaged, it becomes Destroyed instead."
        }
    }

    # -- Ranged Kata --

    # source stat block (page 110)
    #kM1D5gEjY9OhunH7NVxenD ^"Descending Swarm Shot" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Kata"
            ^"Subtype" STRING "Ranged"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "As an Attack action using a readied bow or sling, you may make a TN 3 Martial Arts [Ranged] (Air) check targeting one character within range of the weapon. Reduce the TN of this check by 1 if your target is of silhouette 3 or larger."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, your target becomes vulnerable to attacks by your comrades. When a character makes an Attack action check targeting the affected target, if they succeed, they add one bonus success. This effect persists until the end of your next turn."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op): If you succeed, characters attacking the affected target add bonus successes equal to your ranks in Command instead. (op)(op)+: This effect persists for one additional round per (op)(op) spent this way."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 110)
    #Zes8z1YwjJtEx2DMOYEPQw ^"Thunderbolt Style" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Kata"
            ^"Subtype" STRING "Ranged"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 4
            ^"Activation" STRING "When you make an Attack action check in which you throw your weapon, you may spend (op) as follows:"
            ^"Effects" STRING "(op)+: Choose another character at range 0–1 of your target with vigilance lower than your ranks in Fitness plus (op) spent this way. That character suffers damage equal to your weapon's base damage. You can activate this opportunity multiple times, choosing different characters to affect each time."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW TECHNIQUES - RITUALS
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 110)
    #AWfbgJPwJnfqejeLi6EWT9 ^"Cultural Exchange" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Ritual"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 1
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 2 Culture (Fire) check to establish cultural fundamentals with someone from an unfamiliar culture. A number of characters up to your ranks in Culture can participate in a cultural exchange."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, each participant learns something of value about the culture of each other participant. Even if the participants do not speak the same language, they establish basic communication through gestures and a few learned words."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op): Reduce the TN of any checks you make using the Theorize approach by 1. This effect persists until the end of the next scene."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 111)
    #8guERejPqFVqW8CzwWbiWT ^"Protection of the Flock" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Ritual"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 2 Survival (Fire) check targeting a number of animals up to your ranks in Survival."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, you fortify your targets against disease and other hardship. Until the end of the next scene, they use your ranks in Medicine for any checks they make to resist effects."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): Target an additional number of animals equal to your ranks in Medicine.\n\n(op): If you succeed, each target gains the Emboldened condition (see page 133)."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 111)
    #4koBx0NWeE22JE4qUAzv7C ^"Spiritual Survey" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Ritual"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 3 Survival (Void) check to learn about local spirits and supernatural entities from the natural world around you."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, you learn the nature of the spirits that inhabit the region of the world around you (this effect extends 6 range bands if a specific range is needed). You learn their elemental affinities, any otherworldly realms from which they hail, their preferred offerings, and their general inclinations toward humans. These spirits become aware that someone extended their senses toward them, but not your specific location within the area."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op): The spirits do not become aware that anyone searched for them.\n\n(op)(op): Reduce the TN of any checks you make using the Sense approach by 1. This effect persists until the end of the next scene.\n\n(op)(op)(op): If you a practitioner of meishōdō (if you are trained in the Iuchi Meishōdō Master School or have completed the Student of Names title, page 135), you learn the true name of one spirit of your choice that you have detected in the area."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 112)
    #WZ8xKYctQhHBGSb08Sejh5 ^"Traveler's Experience" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Ritual"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a downtime activity in a place of habitation where you are unfamiliar with the laws and customs (of humans or another sentient species), you may make a TN 2 Culture (Earth) check to observe and determine the customs and protocols of this new place you have reached."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, you quickly ascertain the laws and cultural norms of the place you are currently visiting. You are able to logically discern whether a particular proposed course of action is legal or illegal and whether it is rude or polite."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op): Reduce the TN of any checks you make using the Recall approach by 1. This effect persists until the end of the next scene.\n\n(op)(op): Through study and use of common roots in languages you do speak, you are able to make yourself understood in the common language of the place you are visiting. While you are not fluent in the language, you are intelligible."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 112)
    #viIXOBa8oCx1CTcZ6kqI4p ^"Wayfinder's Instincts" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Ritual"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 2 Survival (Water) check to seek one of the crucial resources for survival. If you are on the ocean, use Seafaring instead of Survival."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, choose one of the following key resources: potable water, food, or shelter. You come upon a sign of the nearest source of that resource, and you are able to determine the direction you must travel to reach it."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): If you succeed, you are able to determine the distance (in days journeyed) to the resource.\n\n(op)(op): Reduce the TN of any checks you make using the Survey approach by 1. This effect persists until the end of the next scene."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 110)
    #lu8CfRSeV4kwwp4747R1sd ^"Center the World" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Ritual"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 3 Survival (Air) check to find a path to civilization even through the most impenetrable desert, densest forest, or most treacherous mountains. If you are on the ocean, use Seafaring instead of Survival."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, you find a sign of the nearest habitation of humans or other sentient beings, and you are able to determine the direction you must travel to reach it."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op)+: Learn one of the following key details about people who inhabit the area you find per (op)(op) spent this way: their culture or national affiliation, their most common means of subsistence, one or more of their commonly used technologies, or the time since they last passed your current location.\n\n(op)(op): Reduce the TN of any checks you make using the Analyze approach by 1. This effect persists until the end of the next scene."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 111)
    #rpxI0yV728lhVlPfVAuEcQ ^"Shadow of Days" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Ritual"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 4 Culture (Earth) check to calculate the distance between two locations. You must have certain information about each location, such as knowledge of which stars are visible there at certain times of year or the length of shadows at certain hours of the day. If you have visited both locations, the TN is 2 instead."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, you determine the distance between the two locations as the crow flies in li, from which you can estimate travel days. The estimate does not necessarily account for all obstacles in the way."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): If you succeed and you have access to a map to cross-compare, you are able to create an even more accurate estimate of the travel time, accounting for known obstacles.\n\n(op)(op): Reduce the TN of any checks you make using the Recall approach by 1. This effect persists until the end of the next scene.\n\n(op)(op)(op): You can accurately predict a future celestial phenomenon, such as the convergence of stellar bodies or an eclipse, in one or both locations."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW TECHNIQUES - SHUJI
    # ===========================

    # -- Air Shūji --

    # source stat block (page 112)
    #TvP2OTi6huL2pGlZOqQwID ^"Cunning Omission" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Air"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Scheme action, you may make a Sentiment (Air) check targeting another character. The TN of this check is equal to your target's focus minus their current strife, to a minimum of 1."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, your target slips up and admits something they were concealing from you. If your target was not concealing anything from you, you now know this fact with certainty."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op)+: If you succeed, your target receives 2 strife per (op)(op) spent this way."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 113)
    #BsPYQ7pYhgaxzeVNprDyWH ^"Entice with Offerings" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Air"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Scheme action, you may make a TN 3 Commerce (Air) check targeting another character. When you use this technique you must give up something you know the target wants: this could mean giving up a physical object your target desires, or making a concession in a negotiation or argument that adds 2 momentum points to your target's current objective."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, you distract your target for one round; during that time, your target cannot add momentum to their social objectives. This effect persists for one round, plus one additional round for every two bonus successes."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op): Instead of being unable to add momentum to their social objectives, when your target would otherwise add one or more momentum points to one of their social objectives, those momentum points are added to one of your social objectives of your choice instead. Your target is not aware that their efforts are being diverted to your cause."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 113)
    #TQKBMiptMmqSRtsQ8rVogY ^"Trader's Intuition" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Air"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Scheme action, you may make a Commerce (Air) check targeting an object you can observe. The TN of the check is 2, or 4 if the object has the Forbidden item quality."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, you assess the target, learning its monetary value and rarity."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): You know a place (which you have visited) where you could sell the object for more money than it is worth in your current location."
        }
    }

    # -- Earth Shūji --

    # source stat block (page 114)
    #CVZ4AAwkwUr1B8pFDPn2yk ^"Cite the Facts" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Earth"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Scheme action check, you may make a Scholar skill (Earth) check targeting another character using a Scholar skill (or other skill, at your GM's discretion) relevant to the topic at hand. The TN of this check is equal to your target's focus minus their current strife, to a minimum of 1."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, your target suffers the Silenced condition unless they choose to gain strife equal to your ranks in Command, plus one for every bonus success."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): If you succeed, add one bonus success to this check for each reserved die you have.\n\n(op)(op)+: Choose one additional target with a focus lower than the original target's per (op)(op) spent this way."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 114)
    #yAc4vdUfB5o54gWHBJUqFZ ^"Solidify Gratitude" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Earth"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Scheme action, you may make a TN 2 Courtesy (Earth) check targeting another character. You can only target a character who has accepted a gift from you this scene or has completed a social objective to which you contributed momentum points."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, you gain the Ally (Target's Name) [Water] advantage (page 101 of the core rulebook) unless your target chooses to forfeit glory equal to the rarity of the gift you gave or to the number of momentum points you contributed to their objective."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op): You learn your target's reason for pursuing their social objective if you do not already know it.\n\n(op)(op): You gain your target's assistance on the next check you make. This effect persists until the end of the scene."
        }
    }

    # -- Fire Shūji --

    # source stat block (page 114)
    #0r8GIosRzsUAzWwWgwKv9P ^"Glorious Entrance" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Fire"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "When you enter a scene, you may make a Performance (Fire) check. The TN of this check is equal to the difference between the glory rank of the character in the scene with the highest glory and your glory rank, to a minimum of 1."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, reduce the TN of Scheme and Support action checks you make by 1. This effect persists for one round, plus one additional round for every two bonus successes."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op)+: When you receive a glory award, increase the amount of glory you gain by 1, plus 1 per additional (op)(op) spent this way.\n\n(op)(op): You gain the Emboldened condition (see page 133)."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 114)
    #Gx7UqC11aieXBQu6Prr3Af ^"Incite Wrath" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Fire"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "When you make a Scheme or Support action check while riding a mount or while you have an animal companion at range 0–1 of you, you may spend (op) as follows:"
            ^"Effects" STRING "(op)(op)+: Your mount or animal companion immediately performs a Strike action targeting one character within range of one of its readied weapons. The damage it deals increases by 1 per (op)(op) spent this way."
        }
    }

    # -- Water Shūji --

    # source stat block (page 115)
    #FI4nQQ3pXWkloDjbYP6e6w ^"Call to Ride" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Water"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 1
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Support action, you can make a TN 1 Survival (Water) check targeting your mount or animal companion, provided it is within range 5 of you."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, your mount or animal companion immediately moves up to 2 range bands toward you, plus 1 additional range band for every two bonus successes. If it is a mount and ends at range 0 of you, you can immediately mount it."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op): Increase the TN of Attack action checks targeting you and your mount or animal companion by 1. This effect persists until the end of your next turn.\n\n(op)(op): If you perform a Maneuver action after mounting, you may move up to 2 range bands instead of 1."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 115)
    #JOnf3GZmEvMPXp7eCksboG ^"Complementary Experience" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Water"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Support action, you may make a TN 3 Command (Water) check targeting one other character in the scene."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, your target has your assistance on the next check they make. This effect persists until the end of your next turn.\n\nIf you succeed, your target may grant you assistance on the next check you make. This effect persists until the end of your next turn."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op): Choose one skill in which you have 0 ranks and your target has 1 or more ranks. When you grant assistance to another character, you count as being trained in that skill. This effect persists until the end of the scene."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 115)
    #sQdYpXf1Ahh8l7WIFqoSkL ^"Horse Whisperer" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Water"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Support action, you may make a Courtesy (Water) or Survival (Water) check targeting a horse or other equine creature that can see or hear you and trusts you. The TN of this check is the target's vigilance."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, you make a wordless request to the target, which they comprehend and are compelled to fulfill. If what they are doing is helpful to your action or to another character's action, that action counts as having assistance. You cannot request something impossible for the target to accomplish. You may put them in harm's way, but if they become injured or harmed, it breaks the trust, and they become immune to this shūji."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op): Give the target the Loyal Steed ability—it can be ridden by a human-sized (silhouette 2 or lower) rider—until the end of the scene."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 115)
    #Pgora3gdYZqyWqOKpEEMIW ^"Everyone Has a Price" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Water"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 4
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Scheme action, you may make a Sentiment (Water) check targeting another character in the scene. The TN of this check is equal to the target's honor rank. You must offer a bribe with a value in koku equal to the target's (intrigue) threat rating to attempt this check. At the GM's discretion, this does not work on mindless or inscrutable Otherworldly creatures, such as undead."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed and your target is a Minion NPC, they accept the bribe and leave the scene.\n\nIf you succeed and your target is not a Minion NPC, they must accept the bribe unless they receive strife equal to your ranks in Courtesy. If they accept the bribe, they must either leave the scene, stop attempting to oppose you, or seek terms with you in some sort of negotiation. At the GM's discretion, this might deescalate a more serious conflict to an intrigue."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): If your target is a Minion NPC, they join your side in the conflict instead of departing."
        }
    }

    # -- Void Shūji --

    #9GbhR8jUu9LFAswOnG7qm1 ^"Appreciate the Scenery" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Void"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 1
            ^"Activation" STRING "When you make a Support action check targeting another character, if you and the character you are targeting are in Dangerous, Entangling, Hallowed, Imbalanced, or Obscuring terrain, you may spend (op) as follows:"
            ^"Effects" STRING "Earth or Water (op): You and your target each remove strife equal to your ranks in Composition.\n\nAir or Fire (op): You and your target gain the Emboldened condition (see page 133).\n\nVoid (op): Your and your target gain the Centered condition (see page 133)."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW INVOCATION
    # ===========================

    #BsXnGLtk9r1ASd3YLCZh0g ^"The World is Not Heavy" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Invocation"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Water"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Support action, you may make a TN 3 Theology (Water) check targeting yourself or a living creature you are touching with your bare hands."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, you augment the target's body with the buoyancy of the water kami. The target gains the ability to carry items with a maximum combined silhouette value equal to the target's own silhouette plus 1. Additionally, their armor loses the Cumbersome item quality while they are wearing it. If the target is a steed, the maximum combined silhouette value of riders it can comfortably carry increases by 2—but none of these riders may individually have a silhouette value greater than the steed can normally carry. These effects persist for the duration of the scene."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "Water (op)+: Increase the maximum combined silhouette value of items the target can carry by 1 per (op) spent.\n\nWater (op)(op): Another item the target has equipped loses the Cumbersome item quality.\n\nWater (op)(op): Increase the maximum combined silhouette value of riders the steed can carry by an additional 2."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW TITLES
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 134)
    #FgINm1rwlpPw8ftOMRBoNc ^"Animal Handler" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Title"
            ^"Assigned By" STRING "The GM, after a character has taken sufficient narrative steps to tame and train a suitable animal. At the bare minimum, this should involve making a successful Survival check as a downtime activity with a TN equal to the animal's combat conflict ranks. One method of obtaining an animal companion is through the Animal Bond passion found in the core rulebook."
            ^"Status Modifier" INTEGER 0
            ^"Glory Modifier" INTEGER 5
            ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 24
            ^"Title Ability" STRING "Instinctive Command: After you perform an action, you may receive 2 fatigue to have any number of your animal companions each take an action that shares a type with your action (your animal's actions are still limited to taking one action of each type per round)."
            ^"Advances" STRING "Trade Skills (skill group), Martial Arts [Unarmed] (skill), Medicine (skill), Sentiment (skill), = Call to Ride (shūji, technique), = Incite Wrath (shūji, technique), = Touchstone of Courage (shūji, technique)"
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 134)
    #QfEK6mmZ9mZobOkKjzBEk8 ^"Doomhunter" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Title"
            ^"Assigned By" STRING "The previous Doomhunter, upon their retirement or impending death"
            ^"Status Modifier" INTEGER 5
            ^"Glory Modifier" INTEGER 20
            ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 28
            ^"Title Ability" STRING "Slayer of Immortals: When you perform an Attack action, you can spend (op) as follows:\n\n(op)+: You attempt to ascertain your target's mortal weaknesses through practiced study of its combat decisions. It must resist with a Sentiment check to conceal the means by which it can be defeated. The TN of this check is equal to your ranks in Survival plus (op) spent this way (Air +2, Fire –2). If your target's check fails, you learn one key clue to defeating it permanently. If you already know how to defeat it, reduce the TN of your next check against it by 2."
            ^"Advances" STRING "Martial Skills (skill group), Skulduggery (skill), Survival (skill), Theology (skill), = Rank 1-2 Rituals (ritual, tech group), = Skulk (ninjutsu, technique), = Soul Sunder (kata, technique)"
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 135)
    #OGAhXuTwNrryXrvO6sU5F3 ^"Imperial Peacekeeper" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Title"
            ^"Assigned By" STRING "A member of the Otomo, Miya, or Seppun family with a status of 65 or higher"
            ^"Status Modifier" INTEGER 5
            ^"Glory Modifier" INTEGER 10
            ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 18
            ^"Title Ability" STRING "By Imperial Command: Once per scene as a Support action, you can choose a number of characters up to your ranks in Command and demand that they pull themselves together. Each chosen character removes 3 strife."
            ^"Advances" STRING "Martial Skills (skill group), Courtesy (skill), Command (skill), Sentiment (skill), = Rank 1-2 Earth Shūji (shūji, tech group), = Cultural Exchange (ritual, technique), = Pillar of Calm (shūji, technique)"
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 135)
    #Fwvpl4N26fV9XBwt7ctKA0 ^"Interpreter" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Title"
            ^"Assigned By" STRING "The GM, after a character has gained an initial familiarity with another culture and desires to learn more."
            ^"Status Modifier" INTEGER 5
            ^"Glory Modifier" INTEGER 5
            ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 12
            ^"Title Ability" STRING "Linguistic Liaison: You learn the languages (written, spoken, signed, and any other forms, as relevant) of the group for which you are an interpreter. Additionally, the first time you make a check to interact socially with a member of this group each encounter, reduce the TN by 1."
            ^"Special" STRING "A character who has completed this title can be assigned it again for a new group. The new instance of the title counts as a different title, which can be completed again, conferring benefits for the new group selected."
            ^"Advances" STRING "Social Skills (skill group), Composition (skill), Culture (skill), Government (skill), = Rank 1 Shūji (shūji, tech group), = Cultural Exchange (ritual, technique), = Traveler's Experience (ritual, technique)"
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 136)
    #z2s5bkh1Vi5VVpoOMXsz5R ^"Scarlet Banners Ranger" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Title"
            ^"Assigned By" STRING "A leader within the White Horde of status 55 or higher"
            ^"Status Modifier" INTEGER 5
            ^"Glory Modifier" INTEGER 10
            ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 24
            ^"Title Ability" STRING "Master of the Lariat: When you make a Martial Arts [Melee] or Martial Arts [Ranged] Attack action check using a Snaring weapon, add 1 kept (skill)(skill) set to (su)(op)."
            ^"Advances" STRING "Martial Skills (skill group), Trade Skills (skill group), Government (skill), Sentiment (skill), = Rank 1-2 Kata (kata, tech group), = Cunning Omission (shūji, technique), = Thunderbolt Style (kata, technique)"
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 136)
    #Wufy1Fhhuc34qeLSzCW6QR ^"Student of Names" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Title"
            ^"Assigned By" STRING "A shugenja trained in Iuchi's method who has a status of 55 or higher, such as the daimyō of the Iuchi family, one of its promising scions, or the ancient and mysterious Grandfather Iuchi."
            ^"Other Requirements" STRING "A character must be capable of performing invocations to receive this title, and they cannot be a member of the Iuchi Meishōdō Master school."
            ^"Status Modifier" INTEGER 5
            ^"Glory Modifier" INTEGER 10
            ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 12
            ^"Title Ability" STRING "Meishōdō Secrets: You are learned in the Way of Names and can wield the sorcerous art called meishōdō. In addition to the new options this grants you in Otherworldly Encounters (see page 125), this title ability lets you sustain one meishōdō talisman of your own creation. If you create a second meishōdō talisman, you must choose one of the two talismans and release the spirit within it."
            ^"Advances" STRING "Command (skill), Culture (skill), Survival (skill), Theology (skill), = Rank 1 Invocations (invocation, tech group), = Spiritual Survey (ritual, technique), = Threshold Barrier (ritual, technique)"
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 137)
    #J2zieRgTzmB24amI5QjXrz ^"White Guard Veteran" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Title"
            ^"Assigned By" STRING "A leader within the White Horde of status 60 or higher"
            ^"Status Modifier" INTEGER 10
            ^"Glory Modifier" INTEGER 15
            ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 32
            ^"Title Ability" STRING "Unrelenting and Inevitable: When you receive strife due to the effect of an Otherworldly or Tainted being, reduce the strife you gain by your ranks in Meditation.\n\nWhen another character makes a check to resist an effect of an Attack action you perform (including a check to resist a critical strike you inflict as part of the attack), increase the TN of the check to resist by 1."
            ^"Advances" STRING "Martial Skills (skill group), Courtesy (skill), Command (skill), Survival (skill), Theology (skill), = A Samurai's Fate (shūji, technique), = Stalking Panther Style (kata, technique), = Sudden Downpour Style (kata, technique)"
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW CONDITIONS
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 133)
    #Ln0IK4uwzwZ1GAg1StPCwU ^"Centered Condition" DEF {

        RULES {
            #bGk8bXNbCpzogBrHCtiF2X: centered "Centered: Description: The character has cleared their mind of distractions and doubts, allowing them to focus on their task.\n\nEffects: When the character makes a check, they may remove up to 2 (st) from the roll results.\n\nRemoved When: At the end of the scene, or after the character benefits from this condition during a check (whichever comes first)."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 133)
    #1lss9pnkcvg1kNXI4upN3R ^"Emboldened Condition" DEF {

        RULES {
            #Hzek6cCeTNdu7M81Iw3xXc: emboldened "Emboldened: Description: The character is filled with the courage to push themself beyond their normal limits and achieve things that might normally be beyond their reach.\n\nEffects: When the character makes a check, they may receive 1 fatigue to keep one additional rolled die.\n\nRemoved When: At the end of the scene, or after the character benefits from this condition during a check (whichever comes first)."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 133)
    #ce445LvL7fAwQMLUSzFzPG ^"Possessed Condition" DEF {

        RULES {
            #t1FETyEP84DngtYbqTUG1p: possessed "Possessed: Description: Willingly or unwillingly, the character has come under the power of a supernatural being, which now exerts a certain influence over their actions.\n\nEffects: When the character becomes Possessed, the possessing spirit states its goal. The character can ignore that goal, but they receive 2 strife at the end of each scene in which they fully disregarded it. When the character becomes Compromised, they must unmask and then attempt to pursue the goal until the end of the scene.\n\nWhen the character makes a check while Possessed, they can use the spirit's skill ranks in place of their own. Additionally, if the spirit knows any invocations or other techniques, the character can use each of these techniques once per scene.\n\nRemoved When: After the character spends a scene pursuing the spirit's goal, they can make a Meditation (Void) check to attempt to expel the spirit. The TN for this check is equal to the spirit's focus. If the character succeeds, the Possession ends, as the spirit is cast out. Possession can also be broken when a character achieves the Dispel Possession social objective (see Otherworldly Encounters on page 125). Alternately, the spirit can choose to end the possession at any time.\n\nAfter this condition is removed, the spirit might physically manifest or might flee into a Spirit Realm, at the GM's discretion."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW DEMEANOR
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 140)
    #RSxZcQpktWGYEJGfAI4gC7 ^"Compassionate Demeanor" DEF {

        RULES {
            #JzazwSpcxDa0Yhmf9Di2sP: compassionate "New Demeanor: Compassionate: The following demeanor is designed to reflect a personality type common among the willful peoples of the Unicorn Clan, along with other samurai who strongly embrace the Bushidō tenet of Jin: Compassion for those of less privileged station, and even for one's enemies. These samurai avoid inflicting needless suffering, believe in social obligation, demonstrate mercy whenever possible, and strive to use their power for the betterment of everyone. The Compassionate demeanor works in the same manner as the other demeanors on page 310 of the core rulebook.\n\nSocial Skill Check TN Modifiers: Fire +2, Air –1, Water –1\n\nCommon Way of Unmasking: Hasty Action\n\nThis person acts immediately on their outrage and frustration, usually without thinking things through. Disregarding any consequences, they attempt the shortest path to what they want, even if they will regret it later."
        }
    }
}
